LISA release_sequence_broken_by_an_add_of_block_scope
(* Block 0 writes data and then releases a flag. An add of block scope in block 1 reads the
   flag. A read in block 1 reads the add and then reads data. The add does not reach block 0, so
   it does not continue the release sequence of the flag. The read of data races.
   Expect: sometimes, a data race. *)
{ data = 0; flag = 0; }
 P0                   | P1                                | P2                    ;
 w[plain] data 1      | rmw[rlx,block] r0 (add r0 1) flag | r[acq,device] r0 flag ;
 w[rel,device] flag 1 |                                   | r[plain] r1 data      ;
scopes: (device (block P0) (block P1 P2))
filter (1:r0 = 1 /\ 2:r0 = 2)
exists (2:r1 = 0)
